WEBVTT

00:07.940 --> 00:08.980
What?

00:08.980 --> 00:10.550
I don't know about that name.

00:10.550 --> 00:11.060
No way.

00:11.060 --> 00:11.830
Why not?

00:11.830 --> 00:14.040
What's wrong with the Glorious Angel?

00:14.040 --> 00:15.630
It sounds skanky.

00:15.630 --> 00:16.940
And totally brainless.

00:16.940 --> 00:18.840
Call it ritzy, at least!

00:18.840 --> 00:20.790
If you're so picky, <i>you</i> suggest something.

00:20.790 --> 00:21.600
What?

00:21.600 --> 00:24.110
How about... the Ātman?

00:24.110 --> 00:25.110
The heck is that?

00:25.110 --> 00:28.540
What about something simple, 
like the Ikebukuro Express?

00:28.540 --> 00:29.620
Right to the point.

00:29.620 --> 00:32.050
Makes it sound faster than it is, though.

00:32.050 --> 00:34.320
Do you have any ideas, Shizuru?

00:35.590 --> 00:37.510
Maybe... the Apogee?

00:37.510 --> 00:38.560
The what G?

00:38.560 --> 00:39.550
Apogee.

00:39.550 --> 00:43.060
The farthest point that the moon 
or a satellite reaches from Earth.

00:43.060 --> 00:44.160
Huh...

00:44.160 --> 00:45.220
Pretty snazzy.

00:45.220 --> 00:46.970
Apogee sounds good to me.

00:46.970 --> 00:47.610
Okay.

00:47.610 --> 00:49.500
Starting today, you're the Apogee.

00:49.500 --> 00:52.570
Shizuru-chan, you're interested 
in stars and outer space?

00:52.570 --> 00:53.240
News to me.

00:54.120 --> 00:56.820
Not me. Yoka.

00:56.820 --> 00:57.730
Yoka-chan?

00:58.260 --> 01:00.000
She taught me the word.

01:00.000 --> 01:01.600
That's still a surprise.

01:01.600 --> 01:06.000
Yoka-chan seemed like she'd be into 
picture books or cutesy stuff.

01:06.000 --> 01:09.680
On that note, why did she go off to Ikebukuro?

01:09.680 --> 01:11.560
All by her lonesome, too.

01:11.560 --> 01:12.900
I know, right?

01:12.900 --> 01:14.660
That's what I've been wondering.

01:14.660 --> 01:18.300
Yoka-chan didn't seem at all like 
someone who'd do stuff on her own.

01:18.300 --> 01:19.480
That's right.

01:19.480 --> 01:22.970
And yet she wandered off 
to Ikebukuro all alone.

01:22.970 --> 01:24.800
That's what's weird—
or, well, hard to explain.

01:24.800 --> 01:26.810
It's a bit of an enigma.

01:26.810 --> 01:27.760
Hmm...

01:27.760 --> 01:29.930
What else is there in Ikebukuro?

01:29.930 --> 01:33.840
They have bookstores, 
an arts theater, an aquarium...

01:33.840 --> 01:35.630
Huh, would she go to any of those?

01:35.630 --> 01:37.250
Doesn't fit my image of her at all.

01:37.250 --> 01:38.460
Yeah, right?

01:38.460 --> 01:42.890
Yoka-chan was the type to fit in 
but never really take charge.

01:42.890 --> 01:44.950
She always hung out in the back with a smile.

01:44.950 --> 01:50.160
Maybe we didn't really know 
much about Yoka-chan at all.

01:50.160 --> 01:51.650
Stop it, Nadeko-chan!

01:51.650 --> 01:53.530
That's too sad to think about!

02:09.310 --> 02:13.070
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

03:26.800 --> 03:31.870
"When it's farthest from the Earth, 
the moon is 400,000 choo-choo..."

03:31.870 --> 03:33.010
Ugh, five minutes!

03:33.010 --> 03:35.200
Seriously, it's never enough!

03:35.990 --> 03:39.180
These rock when you roast them 
and sprinkle some salt on.

03:39.180 --> 03:41.810
If we have leftovers, we can 
make bamboo shoot rice, too.

03:41.810 --> 03:43.230
Pochi-san!

03:43.240 --> 03:44.910
<b>CAUTION: BRIDGE OVERHEAD</b>

03:45.150 --> 03:46.930
Is something wrong, Akira-chan?

03:46.930 --> 03:48.650
Pochi-san just threw up!

03:48.650 --> 03:49.070
What?!

03:50.540 --> 03:52.340
Cats vomit all the time.

03:51.040 --> 03:56.790
Episode 6       Was What I Said That Awful?

03:52.340 --> 03:55.170
It's his first time throwing up 
since we left Agano.

03:55.170 --> 03:56.810
Did he eat something bad?

03:56.810 --> 03:58.670
He's fine.

04:01.040 --> 04:03.550
What if something's wrong with Pochi-san?

04:03.550 --> 04:07.610
We need him to look for Yoka-chan 
when we get to Ikebukuro.

04:07.610 --> 04:10.520
He's the only one who can pick up on her scent.

04:10.520 --> 04:14.100
Which is why we need him to stay healthy!

04:14.100 --> 04:15.750
How old is Pochi-san again?

04:15.750 --> 04:20.490
Pochi-san's been around ever 
since we were kids, right?

04:20.490 --> 04:23.020
That'd make him around 13 or 14 years old?

04:23.020 --> 04:24.680
Whoa, he's a real grandpa!

04:24.680 --> 04:25.530
You're the worst!

04:25.530 --> 04:30.170
Weren't <i>you</i> the one who yelled at me 
when I mentioned Grandma Koyuki's age?!

04:30.170 --> 04:31.680
That was different!

04:31.680 --> 04:32.920
No, it's not!

04:32.920 --> 04:37.130
If Pochi-san dies... he's gone for good!

04:38.220 --> 04:39.870
Hey now, Akira...

04:39.870 --> 04:41.970
It's fine, it's fine.

04:42.440 --> 04:44.310
He's probably just fine.

04:44.310 --> 04:47.100
Shizuru-chan, that wasn't very convincing.

04:47.100 --> 04:48.690
Aren't you worried about him?

04:48.690 --> 04:51.220
You were the one who brought him along.

04:51.220 --> 04:52.370
Hey, hold it.

04:52.370 --> 04:54.500
I didn't drag him along or anything.

04:54.500 --> 04:56.240
Pochi-san decided to follow me.

04:56.980 --> 04:58.930
This again?

04:58.930 --> 05:03.370
Do you want to say that you didn't 
drag us into all of this—

05:03.370 --> 05:05.270
that we decided to follow you here?

05:05.270 --> 05:08.320
Maybe you're right, but that's 
a little insensitive.

05:08.320 --> 05:10.820
I shouldn't have to tell you again.

05:10.820 --> 05:11.500
Um...

05:11.500 --> 05:13.640
Tell me, Shizuru-chan.

05:13.640 --> 05:15.920
Why did Yoka-chan go to Ikebukuro?

05:15.920 --> 05:16.530
What?

05:16.530 --> 05:18.470
I think you must have an idea.

05:18.470 --> 05:19.960
Why ask that now?

05:19.960 --> 05:21.200
Is now a bad time to ask?

05:22.700 --> 05:24.190
Why?

05:24.190 --> 05:26.140
I mean, I can answer...

05:27.860 --> 05:28.750
We had a fight.

05:28.750 --> 05:30.180
Knew it!

05:30.890 --> 05:32.070
About what?

05:32.780 --> 05:34.590
I don't want to talk about it.

05:35.200 --> 05:37.100
I really don't.

05:37.540 --> 05:41.340
You said something to Yoka-chan, 
or did something to her.

05:41.340 --> 05:43.470
What? Yoka-chan got mad at you?

05:43.470 --> 05:45.690
I can't imagine Yoka-chan crying.

05:45.690 --> 05:48.220
I don't really get it myself.

05:48.220 --> 05:49.640
You don't get it?

05:49.640 --> 05:50.920
You did something to her, right?

05:51.530 --> 05:53.370
All she said to me was, "Now I get it."

05:54.530 --> 05:56.330
<i>Whoa, that's a shocker!</i>

05:56.680 --> 05:57.990
You think so?

05:57.990 --> 05:59.140
Totally!

05:59.140 --> 06:00.640
Huh? So what?

06:00.640 --> 06:02.650
By outer space, you mean the stuff up there?

06:02.650 --> 06:04.700
You spend your time thinking 
about that, Yoka?

06:04.700 --> 06:06.520
Never would have guessed!

06:06.520 --> 06:08.490
What do they call that again?

06:08.490 --> 06:09.360
Oh, right.

06:09.360 --> 06:11.040
It was astronomy! Astronomy!

06:11.040 --> 06:16.760
Actually, I want to work on new 
planetary probes and space stations,

06:16.760 --> 06:18.940
developing and simulating 
guidance and control syst—

06:18.350 --> 06:20.990
How do you get a job doing all of that?

06:20.990 --> 06:21.850
Huh?

06:21.850 --> 06:25.230
Study hard at a university, 
write a thesis...

06:25.230 --> 06:26.160
Then what?

06:26.160 --> 06:29.110
Send an application to a research 
center when there's an opening.

06:29.110 --> 06:30.940
An application? That's it?

06:31.700 --> 06:33.480
Yeah, I guess...

06:33.480 --> 06:34.980
Huh...

06:36.800 --> 06:40.470
I'm not sure I totally get it, 
but won't it be super hard?

06:40.470 --> 06:41.440
I know that.

06:41.440 --> 06:43.210
Even so, I still...

06:43.750 --> 06:45.610
You're amazing, Yoka.

06:46.120 --> 06:47.710
No, I'm not.

06:50.320 --> 06:51.910
Man, but... Y'know...

06:51.910 --> 06:53.210
Outer space? Probes?

06:53.210 --> 06:56.340
I'd never even consider 
doing that for a living.

06:56.340 --> 06:58.010
How do you even come up with that?

06:58.550 --> 06:59.860
Honestly, though?

06:59.860 --> 07:02.550
It doesn't sound very realistic to me.

07:02.550 --> 07:03.720
Realistic?

07:03.720 --> 07:05.170
All that stuff.

07:05.170 --> 07:06.470
All that stuff...

07:06.470 --> 07:09.270
I mean, we're just regular folks.

07:09.270 --> 07:13.490
I figure that kinda stuff is best saved 
for people who are more exceptional.

07:13.490 --> 07:16.750
Oh, I'm not trying to make 
fun of you or anything.

07:16.750 --> 07:21.310
But this is some real far-fetched stuff 
you're talking about.

07:21.310 --> 07:22.330
Is it really?

07:22.330 --> 07:23.820
Totally!

07:23.820 --> 07:26.770
Going from Agano to the stars, 
outer space, the galaxy?

07:26.770 --> 07:27.930
No way! Not happening!

07:27.930 --> 07:30.430
You're just embarrassing yourself 
with such high hopes.

07:30.430 --> 07:33.450
You need to accept reality 
and compromise a little.

07:33.450 --> 07:34.470
C'mon, now!

07:34.470 --> 07:36.260
How about something more normal?

07:36.260 --> 07:37.590
Normal's all you'll ever be,

07:37.590 --> 07:41.110
so do you really need to worry about 
all this exceptional-people stuff?

07:41.110 --> 07:44.470
I mean, I think it's great that 
you're thinking about all that,

07:44.470 --> 07:46.310
but it'll be rough when you don't make it.

07:46.310 --> 07:48.850
Like, you gotta know 
you've got no chance, right?

07:48.850 --> 07:50.220
Well, not like I would either.

07:50.220 --> 07:51.660
Guess we're the same.

07:53.750 --> 07:54.800
What's up?

07:54.800 --> 07:56.010
What do you mean?

07:56.010 --> 07:57.930
You suddenly went quiet.

07:57.930 --> 07:59.700
Did I say something weird?

08:00.230 --> 08:01.350
Not really.

08:01.350 --> 08:02.920
It's just that now I get it.

08:02.920 --> 08:04.440
Get what, exactly?

08:04.440 --> 08:08.190
If you have a problem with what 
I said, say it to my face!

08:08.190 --> 08:09.850
You're entitled to your opinion.

08:09.850 --> 08:12.310
You're really pushing me away, huh?

08:12.310 --> 08:13.220
Insensitive much?

08:13.490 --> 08:16.580
I don't think I said anything wrong here.

08:19.040 --> 08:20.470
I see now.

08:21.060 --> 08:23.380
So that's what you're like, Shizuru.

08:23.770 --> 08:24.630
Huh?

08:24.630 --> 08:26.620
What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?

08:26.620 --> 08:28.690
I could say the same about you, Yoka!

08:29.020 --> 08:30.450
That's right.

08:30.970 --> 08:33.260
This is how I am.

08:33.770 --> 08:34.610
Sorry!

08:35.490 --> 08:36.980
What are you sorry about?!

08:37.280 --> 08:40.540
I don't care about you anymore, Yoka!

08:41.240 --> 08:44.280
I think you're to blame here, Shizuru-chan.

08:44.280 --> 08:47.890
I'd feel so awful and angry 
if you put me down like that.

08:47.890 --> 08:50.670
Especially for laughing 
at the things I like.

08:50.670 --> 08:51.480
I know—

08:51.480 --> 08:55.340
Shizuru-chan already realizes 
that she said some awful things.

08:56.260 --> 08:57.770
Did I really?

08:58.650 --> 09:00.900
Was what I said that awful?

09:00.900 --> 09:04.830
Well, that's the whole reason Yoka-chan 
went to Ikebukuro on her own, isn't it?

09:04.830 --> 09:06.650
Why Ikebukuro, though?

09:06.650 --> 09:08.420
Beats me. I wonder why.

09:08.420 --> 09:10.450
Hey, why Ikebukuro?

09:10.450 --> 09:11.470
I don't know.

09:11.470 --> 09:15.740
But your fight is the reason 
Yoka-chan ran away from Agano.

09:15.740 --> 09:17.410
I don't think you can deny that.

09:17.410 --> 09:20.940
Even if you don't think 
you said anything wrong,

09:20.940 --> 09:24.990
if Yoka-chan ended up being 
hurt by it, then that's wrong.

09:24.990 --> 09:26.140
Hold on.

09:26.140 --> 09:29.760
Shizuru-chan, don't you want to find 
Yoka-chan and apologize to her?

09:29.760 --> 09:30.980
Still...

09:30.980 --> 09:33.750
Isn't Yoka just as bad for leaving 
without so much as a word?

09:35.510 --> 09:38.620
Well, let's just say both of you 
are partly to blame.

09:39.010 --> 09:42.700
I can't say much, since this 
is a matter between you two,

09:42.700 --> 09:46.680
but I'm disappointed that you 
couldn't tell us this until now.

09:46.680 --> 09:48.040
Oh, yeah!

09:48.040 --> 09:48.680
Yep.

09:48.680 --> 09:51.830
I'm not sure why you kept it a secret from us.

09:51.830 --> 09:52.770
A sense of guilt?

09:52.770 --> 09:53.990
Not really.

09:53.990 --> 09:56.570
It's not like I dragged you 
all out here with me.

09:56.570 --> 09:58.180
There you go again!

09:57.400 --> 09:58.400
Really?!

09:58.400 --> 09:59.560
Don't give us that!

09:59.560 --> 10:03.160
Shizuru-chan, do you think of us 
as a bother for tagging along?

10:03.450 --> 10:05.910
I thought we all wanted to go 
to Ikebukuro together.

10:05.910 --> 10:07.820
Are you saying you don't feel that way?

10:07.820 --> 10:11.690
I just wanted to go to Ikebukuro. That's all.

10:11.690 --> 10:13.870
All by yourself, you mean?

10:14.460 --> 10:15.640
Yeah, maybe!

10:15.640 --> 10:16.810
What? Seriously?!

10:16.810 --> 10:18.220
A little late for that!

10:18.220 --> 10:20.350
Okay, sorry. You're right.

10:20.350 --> 10:22.870
Yeah, maybe I'm better off alone.

10:22.870 --> 10:24.550
Maybe we're all better off.

10:25.850 --> 10:27.650
Shizuru-chan, what are you doing?

10:27.650 --> 10:28.600
Leaving.

10:28.600 --> 10:29.360
I'll go by myself.

10:29.360 --> 10:29.870
What?!

10:29.870 --> 10:30.600
Sorry.

10:31.720 --> 10:33.630
Wait, right now?!

10:33.630 --> 10:35.110
It's dark outside!

10:35.110 --> 10:36.270
Hey!

10:36.270 --> 10:37.500
Stop her, Nadeko-chan!

10:37.500 --> 10:39.360
She's going off by herself!

10:40.300 --> 10:42.450
Maybe she just needs to calm down.

10:42.450 --> 10:43.410
What?

10:43.410 --> 10:44.890
You're going to let her go?

10:44.890 --> 10:47.370
Would forcing her to come back 
really be better?

10:47.370 --> 10:48.690
Well...

10:48.690 --> 10:50.270
She needs time to cool off.

10:50.620 --> 10:51.760
And so do we.

10:56.020 --> 10:57.120
Pochi-san?

10:57.120 --> 10:59.010
You're going with Shizuru-chan?

10:59.010 --> 11:00.620
What? Don't go!

11:01.570 --> 11:05.450
Pochi-san will do something 
about Shizuru-chan.

11:05.450 --> 11:06.900
Really?

11:12.490 --> 11:14.260
Pochi-san.

11:14.260 --> 11:15.770
Go back with the others.

11:15.770 --> 11:18.200
They'll say I dragged you along with me again.

11:19.710 --> 11:21.110
Guess they didn't say that.

11:21.110 --> 11:23.270
I'm fine, really.

11:23.960 --> 11:26.130
You're here of your own will!

11:26.130 --> 11:28.130
I'm insensitive, you know!

11:30.150 --> 11:31.650
Let's eat dinner.

11:31.650 --> 11:32.520
I don't get it.

11:32.520 --> 11:35.210
How can you stay so calm, Nadeko-chan?!

11:35.210 --> 11:36.190
Reimi-chan.

11:36.190 --> 11:39.710
I won't answer you if you're just trying 
to take your anger out on me.

11:42.680 --> 11:44.050
I'm sorry.

11:44.050 --> 11:49.240
It was about 65% anger, 
but 35% of me really wants to know.

11:49.240 --> 11:50.600
Think about it.

11:50.600 --> 11:54.040
The only way to get to Ikebukuro 
is along the train tracks.

11:54.040 --> 11:56.150
And there's only one set of tracks.

11:56.150 --> 11:59.620
As long as we follow this path, 
we're sure to catch up to Shizuru-chan.

11:59.620 --> 12:00.370
Oh, you're right!

12:00.780 --> 12:02.060
Nadeko-chan.

12:02.060 --> 12:03.840
You looked really scary there for a moment.

12:03.840 --> 12:05.450
What? Really?

12:08.460 --> 12:10.450
Let's eat up so we can all feel better.

12:10.790 --> 12:12.410
Time to dig in!

12:14.760 --> 12:15.540
You know what?

12:15.540 --> 12:19.620
When it comes down to it, 
the Apogee here is Shizuru-chan's train.

12:19.620 --> 12:21.920
She could have called it the Perigee.

12:21.920 --> 12:22.980
The what G?

12:22.980 --> 12:23.840
Perigee.

12:23.840 --> 12:27.040
Apogee is when the moon is 
farthest away from the Earth,

12:27.040 --> 12:28.520
and perigee is when it's the closest.

12:28.520 --> 12:30.590
The distance between 
Shizuru-chan and Yoka-chan?

12:30.590 --> 12:31.600
I can't say for sure.

12:32.010 --> 12:34.670
But since we're on our way to meet her,

12:34.670 --> 12:38.390
giving it a faraway name, instead 
of a close one, feels a bit wrong.

12:38.390 --> 12:40.110
A little, yeah.

12:40.870 --> 12:41.980
More rice!

12:41.980 --> 12:43.160
What? That was quick!

12:43.160 --> 12:44.830
Yay! First come, first served!

12:44.830 --> 12:45.690
You'll get fat.

12:45.690 --> 12:46.400
What?

12:46.400 --> 12:48.910
Don't be mean to her!

12:55.630 --> 12:57.610
I don't want to take the long way.

12:58.430 --> 13:00.170
Shortcut time!

13:01.090 --> 13:02.370
Next stop is Kiyose, huh?

13:02.370 --> 13:03.420
We'll get there in no time.

13:04.130 --> 13:06.780
We need to hurry as much 
as we can to Ikebukuro.

13:08.600 --> 13:10.490
We'll stay here for the night,

13:10.490 --> 13:12.590
and set off tomorrow in the morning.

13:12.590 --> 13:16.820
It'll be awkward if we catch up 
to Shizuru-chan right away.

13:16.820 --> 13:17.850
For all of us.

13:19.950 --> 13:21.850
I forgive Shizuru-chan.

13:22.330 --> 13:23.590
What's this now?

13:23.590 --> 13:25.420
We're friends, aren't we?

13:25.420 --> 13:29.390
Does that mean Yoka-chan's not her friend, 
because they never made up?

13:29.390 --> 13:31.080
Huh? Um...

13:31.080 --> 13:31.870
That's not right.

13:32.260 --> 13:35.410
Fighting and making up 
are both part of being friends.

13:35.700 --> 13:39.030
But you stop seeing each other 
if you never make up.

13:39.030 --> 13:40.700
Are you still friends?

13:40.700 --> 13:42.470
Even if you never see each other again?

13:43.570 --> 13:44.940
No more, no more!

13:44.940 --> 13:48.140
Thinking about hard stuff right before bed 
will give you nightmares!

13:48.750 --> 13:50.210
That's weird.

13:50.210 --> 13:53.070
We should have been out of there 
in an hour or so,

13:53.070 --> 13:54.620
but we've been climbing for three hours.

13:54.620 --> 13:56.470
Is it supposed to take this long?

13:56.470 --> 13:57.590
No way, right?

13:58.190 --> 13:59.420
Pochi-san.

13:59.420 --> 14:00.910
Where's your response?

14:00.910 --> 14:03.980
If I talk to myself, that just 
makes me a weirdo.

14:06.380 --> 14:08.080
I'm stupid.

14:08.080 --> 14:09.980
Why am I so stupid?

14:11.630 --> 14:13.380
Would it be best to go back?

14:13.380 --> 14:14.790
Should I?

14:20.770 --> 14:21.950
I've made up my mind.

14:21.950 --> 14:22.710
Let's go back.

14:24.920 --> 14:25.560
Huh?

14:26.490 --> 14:28.000
Which way was it again?

14:30.680 --> 14:34.670
When you find yourself lost, 
the number-one rule is to climb up, not down!

14:43.590 --> 14:44.670
Pochi-san?

14:46.880 --> 14:49.880
What's that weird smell?

14:53.730 --> 14:54.880
Hey, Pochi...

14:54.880 --> 14:55.790
Huh?

14:56.810 --> 14:57.580
Poch—

15:07.980 --> 15:09.250
Seriously?!

15:09.830 --> 15:11.210
Pochi-san!

15:12.970 --> 15:14.970
Where are you all from?!

15:14.970 --> 15:16.600
Is it Kiyose?!

15:22.260 --> 15:24.230
Don't mess with Agano jiu-jitsu!

15:26.760 --> 15:27.850
Pochi-san!

15:33.050 --> 15:34.410
Hey! Go away!

15:34.410 --> 15:35.960
Shut up!

15:40.500 --> 15:41.210
Halt.

15:50.910 --> 15:52.590
The first one in ages.

15:56.980 --> 15:58.390
Let's bring her along.

16:00.270 --> 16:02.220
Hey, hold it right there!

16:02.220 --> 16:03.510
Pipe down.

16:11.170 --> 16:12.680
I don't see her.

16:12.680 --> 16:14.810
Did we miss her somewhere?

16:14.810 --> 16:16.160
Maybe we passed her.

16:16.480 --> 16:18.690
We've been going pretty slowly, though.

16:18.690 --> 16:19.410
We have.

16:19.870 --> 16:23.160
Nadeko-chan, what if Shizuru-chan 
strayed from the tracks?

16:23.580 --> 16:26.500
And if she did, where did it happen?

16:26.500 --> 16:27.390
Yeah, where?

16:27.390 --> 16:28.920
I'm the one asking here.

16:28.920 --> 16:30.680
It's not like I know, either.

16:30.680 --> 16:32.420
Should we go back?

16:32.420 --> 16:32.970
What?!

16:32.970 --> 16:34.010
Keep going, then?

16:34.010 --> 16:35.670
We've come pretty far since morning.

16:35.670 --> 16:38.350
Nadeko-chan said to calm down, right?

16:38.350 --> 16:41.130
What if Shizuru-chan 
calmed down and came back?

16:41.130 --> 16:41.810
Back where?

16:41.810 --> 16:43.810
Where we were when she ran off.

16:43.810 --> 16:45.900
Who would run off and then come right back?

16:45.900 --> 16:47.380
You never know, do you?

16:47.380 --> 16:48.920
We're talking about Shizuru-chan.

16:48.920 --> 16:49.530
Ah...

16:49.800 --> 16:53.450
We don't know whether Shizuru-chan 
would follow the tracks to begin with.

16:53.450 --> 16:56.150
The roads are more dangerous 
than the tracks.

16:56.150 --> 16:57.660
Yeah...

16:57.660 --> 16:59.840
But this is Shizuru-chan 
we're talking about.

17:02.040 --> 17:03.320
Huh? Huh?

17:03.320 --> 17:03.910
What?

17:03.910 --> 17:04.670
Be quiet!

17:04.670 --> 17:05.470
What now?!

17:09.920 --> 17:11.190
No way!

17:11.190 --> 17:12.780
It's the Black Leopard caravan!

17:12.780 --> 17:14.170
It's Neko-nii and his crew!

17:19.150 --> 17:20.540
What's your name?

17:20.540 --> 17:22.130
Chikura Shizuru.

17:22.130 --> 17:23.580
A second-year at Agano High School.

17:23.580 --> 17:24.720
Agano High, huh?

17:24.720 --> 17:26.730
I'm Kuroki Mito.

17:26.730 --> 17:28.350
You can call me Kuroki-san.

17:28.350 --> 17:31.230
Kuroki...san, you're a zombie, right?

17:31.230 --> 17:32.130
What's this now?

17:32.130 --> 17:33.300
Ah, well...

17:33.300 --> 17:37.170
Just wondering why you're 
the only one who can talk.

17:39.560 --> 17:43.330
Why can I talk, you ask? 
Because I'm the queen of the zombies.

17:43.760 --> 17:45.880
The queen of the zombies?!

17:45.880 --> 17:47.580
Ikebukuro by train?

17:47.580 --> 17:49.380
What a reckless idea.

17:49.380 --> 17:50.480
Hey, Neko-nii-san.

17:50.480 --> 17:51.960
Do you have any more news for us?

17:51.960 --> 17:53.330
The latest Ikebukuro news.

17:53.330 --> 17:57.490
The latest I have is pretty old now.

17:57.490 --> 17:58.960
And it's all second-hand.

17:58.960 --> 18:00.180
That's totally fine.

18:00.650 --> 18:04.440
Well, Agano's pretty weird, 
but Ikebukuro's even worse.

18:04.440 --> 18:08.620
Like being stretched out into billboards, 
or turned into egg custard and steamed.

18:08.620 --> 18:09.240
What?

18:09.240 --> 18:11.040
You're not making any sense.

18:11.040 --> 18:12.150
I figured you'd say that.

18:12.150 --> 18:12.870
Um...

18:12.870 --> 18:17.490
Is it true that the world outside of the 
Seibu Ikebukuro line doesn't exist?

18:17.490 --> 18:21.150
I can't say for certain, 
since I haven't looked into it myself.

18:21.150 --> 18:23.380
That said, I can't deny the possibility.

18:23.380 --> 18:26.870
Especially with what I've heard from 
those searching for other rail lines.

18:26.870 --> 18:30.070
You'll be looping back 
around after this, right?

18:30.070 --> 18:31.210
Huh? Yeah.

18:31.210 --> 18:34.450
If you see Shizuru-chan in a town, 
or while moving as a caravan,

18:34.450 --> 18:39.290
tell her she can come back any time, 
and that we'll be waiting.

18:39.290 --> 18:42.140
That's fine by me... if I can find her.

18:42.140 --> 18:44.610
Hey, can't you be a little more confident?

18:44.610 --> 18:47.220
I'm sure you've all seen already,

18:47.220 --> 18:50.970
but 7G turned the world into 
an incredibly vast expanse.

18:51.270 --> 18:53.740
The possibility of running 
into a specific person...

18:54.330 --> 18:58.480
Ikebukuro's a gauntlet, but this 
area shows signs of danger, too.

18:58.480 --> 19:00.160
You girls should leave as soon as you can.

19:00.460 --> 19:01.830
What's the danger?

19:01.830 --> 19:03.080
Zombies.

19:03.080 --> 19:05.110
You mean corpses of the undead variety?

19:05.400 --> 19:08.450
We've just received eyewitness 
reports of migratory zombies.

19:09.690 --> 19:11.420
Migratory zombies?

19:11.420 --> 19:13.920
Zombies are surprisingly fragile.

19:13.920 --> 19:16.940
They rot in the heat 
and freeze and snap in the cold.

19:15.960 --> 19:17.630
<b>Extra-Strong
Deodorizer
Fefreze</b>

19:16.940 --> 19:21.200
They get mushy in the rain, 
but they can't dry out too much, either.

19:21.200 --> 19:22.600
Makes sense.

19:22.600 --> 19:27.050
That's why they're constantly on the move, 
searching for the perfect climate and soil.

19:27.050 --> 19:28.320
I see.

19:28.320 --> 19:30.110
I act as their compass.

19:30.110 --> 19:33.070
As the queen, I have a duty to lead them.

19:33.070 --> 19:34.850
I understand now.

19:34.860 --> 19:42.570
<b></b>Offerings

19:35.120 --> 19:36.520
You seem listless.

19:36.520 --> 19:37.870
Are you hungry?

19:37.870 --> 19:40.410
Huh? Yes, I suppose.

19:40.410 --> 19:42.580
For now, give her a part to eat.

19:42.870 --> 19:44.050
A part?

19:44.050 --> 19:45.330
Huh? P-Part?

19:46.610 --> 19:47.700
Eat up.

19:47.700 --> 19:49.180
Help yourself.

19:49.180 --> 19:50.290
Oh, um...

19:50.290 --> 19:54.570
I try to avoid stuff like beef jerky 
because it gets stuck in my teeth.

19:54.570 --> 19:55.810
I see.

19:55.810 --> 19:56.380
What about you?

19:56.660 --> 19:57.710
Want some?

20:00.170 --> 20:01.680
Guess he doesn't.

20:04.330 --> 20:07.410
So <i>does</i> it taste like dried meat?

20:07.410 --> 20:08.550
I wouldn't know.

20:08.550 --> 20:10.460
I've never had any.

20:10.460 --> 20:10.930
What?

20:10.930 --> 20:12.700
I'm the queen.

20:12.700 --> 20:14.820
I have my own special diet.

20:13.980 --> 20:15.360
<b>Yasaka's
\h\h\hCorned Beef</b>

20:15.590 --> 20:17.560
Sorry I can't join you.

20:17.560 --> 20:19.430
I've got my own work to do.

20:19.430 --> 20:20.990
Oh, no! It's fine.

20:20.990 --> 20:22.030
Be careful.

20:22.030 --> 20:25.190
If you run into zombies, 
the best thing to do is just stay still.

20:25.570 --> 20:29.030
The trick I mentioned is 
nothing more than a theory.

20:30.600 --> 20:32.040
Zombies...

20:32.040 --> 20:32.850
Those things, right?

20:32.850 --> 20:36.140
Drooping eyeballs, rotting flesh, 
eats brains, bites people?

20:36.140 --> 20:37.210
That's pretty much it.

20:37.210 --> 20:39.480
If you get bitten by a zombie, 
you turn into one?

20:39.480 --> 20:40.340
Usually, yeah.

20:40.340 --> 20:43.110
What do we do if Shizuru becomes a zombie?

20:43.110 --> 20:45.270
You see pretty smart ones nowadays

20:45.270 --> 20:48.350
that retain their personality 
from before they died.

20:48.350 --> 20:49.570
So they don't attack?

20:49.570 --> 20:50.340
They do.

20:51.980 --> 20:53.220
Neko-nii-san!

20:53.530 --> 20:55.670
We should go with Neko-nii-san!

20:55.670 --> 20:57.460
We might still be able to catch up!

20:57.460 --> 20:59.260
Wait, what about Shizuru-chan?!

20:59.260 --> 21:03.860
If Shizuru-chan's a zombie, being with 
Neko-nii-san would be better and safer!

21:03.860 --> 21:07.740
Reimi-chan, are you saying you'd abandon 
Shizuru-chan if she was a zombie?

21:07.740 --> 21:09.530
She wouldn't be your friend anymore?

21:09.530 --> 21:11.370
She's my friend but also a zombie!

21:11.370 --> 21:13.170
She's a zombie but also our friend!

21:13.940 --> 21:17.000
She'd still be our friend 
as a zombie... I think.

21:18.300 --> 21:19.680
You know...

21:19.680 --> 21:22.210
If a woman's dating 
a terrible guy and she says,

21:22.210 --> 21:26.220
"He's a good person, when he's 
not gambling or drinking"...

21:26.480 --> 21:31.810
You know how everyone responds, 
"He does drink, which makes him bad"?

21:32.680 --> 21:34.930
Is that what we're talking about here?

21:35.330 --> 21:36.670
No...

21:36.670 --> 21:38.090
Not really.

21:38.090 --> 21:39.650
Actually, it's the opposite!

21:39.650 --> 21:41.360
"He's such a slob, but I love him!"

21:41.360 --> 21:43.800
Or, "He's so selfish, but I forgive him!"

21:43.800 --> 21:47.920
You mean like, "She's <i>such</i> a zombie, 
but she's still my friend"?

21:48.320 --> 21:52.080
"Shizuru-chan said all those awful things, 
but she's still my friend!"

21:52.080 --> 21:54.160
Do you think that's what Yoka-chan thinks?

21:54.740 --> 21:56.300
She does.

21:56.300 --> 21:57.830
I'm sure she does.

21:58.440 --> 22:01.330
We'll need to bring Shizuru-chan 
to Yoka-chan to find out!

22:01.330 --> 22:02.340
Yeah!
